<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Marlin year earnings jump, no dividend.</title>
<headline>Marlin year earnings jump, no dividend.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     5.0	   vs 0.2</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-exceps (cts) 5.0	   vs 2.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   9.0	   vs 0.2</p>
<p>    Operating profit	14.8	  vs 5.4</p>
<p>    Finance charges	  5.3	  vs 3.7</p>
<p>Profit after tax,</p>
<p>     finance charges	 9.5	  vs 1.7</p>
<p>    Minorities		(0.5)	 vs 0.1</p>
<p>    Exceptional costs	-	    vs 1.6</p>
<p>    Turnover		 156.8	  vs 86.3</p>
<p>Full name: Marlin Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Granite producer Marlin said it sold 20,434 cubic metres at an average price of $729 fob.</p>
<p>Turnover increased largely as a result of the incorporation of Minaco Granite and Marble Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
